1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:03,666
Here's how to reverse engineer PandaDoc from a written spec.

2
00:00:03,666 --> 00:00:08,347
We gave Claude one Markdown file, and checked twenty-nine things in a real browser.

3
00:00:08,347 --> 00:00:10,298
Here's what passed, and what broke.

4
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:15,185
The spec copies the quoting part of PandaDoc a small sales team uses.

5
00:00:15,185 --> 00:00:17,461
A price list, so prices stay the same.

6
00:00:17,461 --> 00:00:20,263
Line items with discounts, tax and live totals.

7
00:00:20,263 --> 00:00:22,072
Templates for common packages.

8
00:00:22,072 --> 00:00:25,807
And a client link, where the buyer accepts by typing their name.

9
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,510
The core rule is discount approval.

10
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:30,632
Take Lee's quote for Ridgeway Partners.

11
00:00:30,632 --> 00:00:33,815
The list price is seventeen thousand, four hundred dollars.

12
00:00:33,815 --> 00:00:37,052
Twenty percent off a hundred seats takes off three thousand.

13
00:00:37,052 --> 00:00:43,153
That's seventeen point two percent, over the fifteen percent limit, so a manager must approve it before it's sent.

14
00:00:43,153 --> 00:00:45,434
And no manager can approve their own quote.

15
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:49,132
Claude built it in four phases, one prompt each.

16
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:52,621
The foundation, with clients, the price list and settings.

17
00:00:52,621 --> 00:00:53,804
Quotes and pricing.

18
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,111
Approval, sending and the client page.

19
00:00:56,111 --> 00:00:58,241
Then expiry, printing and invoices.

20
00:00:58,241 --> 00:01:01,671
Every check ran in a real browser, on freshly seeded data.

21
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:03,686
Here's what it built.

22
00:01:03,686 --> 00:01:07,677
The quotes home shows open quotes, approvals waiting, and the win rate.

23
00:01:07,677 --> 00:01:13,220
The editor keeps list prices fixed, updates totals live, and warns when a discount needs a manager.

24
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:16,324
The manager sees the approval request beside the quote.

25
00:01:16,324 --> 00:01:18,652
Templates make common packages one click.

26
00:01:18,652 --> 00:01:22,033
And on a phone, the client accepts by typing their full name.

27
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:29,129
In the final run, on a fresh database, all twenty-nine checks passed, along with forty-seven automated tests.

28
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:32,139
But the more useful result is what broke.

29
00:01:32,139 --> 00:01:34,345
The build exposed eight gaps in the spec.

30
00:01:34,345 --> 00:01:36,131
Places where Claude had to guess.

31
00:01:36,131 --> 00:01:39,702
Sign-in matched people by email, but the seed people had no emails.

32
00:01:39,702 --> 00:01:43,273
Duplicate didn't say what gets copied, like the discount and notes.

33
00:01:43,273 --> 00:01:48,000
And when no other manager could approve, the spec didn't say if the request went through.

34
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,838
Every gap is now fixed in the spec.

35
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:53,933
Passing every check isn't the same as production-ready.

36
00:01:53,933 --> 00:02:00,944
We didn't test real sign-in, sending email, the daily job on a real scheduler, the browser's print dialog, or hosting.

37
00:02:00,944 --> 00:02:04,008
Those are yours to check before a team relies on it.

38
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:06,074
So is it worth building?

39
00:02:06,074 --> 00:02:10,356
PandaDoc Starter is nineteen dollars per seat per month, with up to five templates.

40
00:02:10,356 --> 00:02:11,579
Business is forty-nine.

41
00:02:11,579 --> 00:02:16,370
For a team of ten on Business, that's five thousand, eight hundred and eighty dollars a year.

42
00:02:16,370 --> 00:02:20,396
If you need legally binding e-signatures, payments, or CRM sync, use PandaDoc.

43
00:02:20,396 --> 00:02:25,646
If you send a few quotes a week, you mostly need the price list, the approval rule, and an accept link.

44
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:27,477
The spec is free.

45
00:02:27,477 --> 00:02:34,612
The data model, sixteen rules, seed data, four phase prompts, and all twenty-nine checks, with the eight fixes already in.

46
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:37,222
Find it at personal software factory dot com.
